@@FN@@
===
'Theorie gedeckter cylindrischer und conischer Pfeifen und der Querflöten,' Schweiger, *Journ.* lxviii. 1833, is disfigured by misprints so that the formulæ are unintelligible, and the theory is also extremely hazardous. But they are the only papers I have found, @@FN@@
>>>
<<<
@@FN@@
===
and are referred to by Theobald Boehm, *Ueber den Flötenbau*, Mainz, 1847. An English version of this, by himself, made for Mr. Rudall in 1847, has recently been edited with additional letters by W. S. Broadwood, and published by Rudall, Carte, & Co., makers of his flutes. @@FN@@
>>>
<<<
@@FN@@
===
See also Victor Mahillon, *Étude sur le doigté de la Flûte Boehm*, 1882, and a paper by M. Aristide Cavaillé-Coll, in *L'Écho Musical* for 11 Jan. 1883.—*Translator*.

